  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera reports that an Eisenkot ally was elected Knesset speaker with the backing of the Arab bloc.",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:3f09e69b3a19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Lauder told Haaretz in October 2026 that he spent about 10 to 15 months traveling between Israel, Syria and Lebanon, working with Assad and Rafic Hariri on a ten-point peace framework.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386180672:106"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Benjamin \"Bibi\" Netanyahu (born 21 October 1949) is an Israeli politician and diplomat who has served as prime minister of Israel since 2022.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386180672:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Benjamin Netanyahu was born on 21 October 1949 in Tel Aviv.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q43723:P569",
        "wd:Q43723:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "He was educated at Cheltenham High School, MIT Sloan School of Management and Massachusetts Institute of Technology.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q43723:P69:Q5090207",
        "wd:Q43723:P69:Q142740",
        "wd:Q43723:P69:Q49108"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:38Z",
      "text": "He later worked for Boston Consulting Group, in Jerusalem.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q43723:P108:Q135635",
        "wd:Q43723:P937:Q1218"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "5 awards are on record, among them the Irving Kristol Award in 2015 and the Grand Cross of the Order of the Southern Cross in 2019.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q43723:P166:Q6074664",
        "wd:Q43723:P166:Q22058319"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "His notable works include A Place Among the Nations, Fighting Terrorism and Bibi: My Story.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q43723:P800:Q16133305",
        "wd:Q43723:P800:Q20502069",
        "wd:Q43723:P800:Q114244190"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:07Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined the story: “Eisenkot ally elected Knesset speaker with Arab bloc’s backing”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:3f09e69b3a19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:14Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined its report: “Israeli parliament elects speaker backed by Netanyahu opponents”.",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:09b6db0d2eac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:23Z",
      "text": "Sources include Al Jazeera and France 24, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
